 I'd be happy to help you write a function to sort the keys of a JSON object in JavaScript! Here's an example of how you can do it using the `Object.entries()` method and the `Array.prototype.sort()` method:

```javascript
function sortJsonKeys(jsonObj) {
  // First, convert the JSON object to an array of key-value pairs using Object.entries()
  const entries = Object.entries(jsonObj);

  // Next, sort the array using Array.prototype.sort() with a custom compare function that sorts based on your desired order (assuming you want alphabetical order here)
  entries.sort((a, b) => {
    return a[0].localeCompare(b[0]);
  });

  // Finally, use Object.fromEntries() to convert the sorted array back into a JSON object
  return Object.fromEntries(entries);
}

// Example usage:
const jsonObj = { b: "two", a: "one" };
console.log(sortJsonKeys(jsonObj)); // Output: { a: 'one', b: 'two' }
```

